  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Enhanced the capacity of RSE &quot;Kazvodkhoz&quot; to meet the demand of water users. 
- Elaborated several economic incentives to comprehend water sector of Kazakhstan
- Piloted/demonstrated innovative water measurment and operational systems which ensures the efficient water supply in Kazakhstan
- Enahnced capacity and awareness raised of the local community of water e billing and measurement devices.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2017">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Lower capacity of RSE &quot;Kazvodkhoz&quot;  to deliver sufficient irrigation water to the water users. 
- Absence of efficient economic mechanism to provide incentive for development of water sector in Kazakhstan. 
- Absence of innovative water measurement devices and respective operational system is in place to ensure transparant irrigation water delivery. 
- Lower capacity and unawreness of the local community on innovative water billing and measurement devices.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	Provide technical support to RSE Kazvodkhoz to develop a national development plan for RSE Kazvodkhoz 2020-2030. 
2.	Design and develop a concept for irrigation water automation.
3.	Develop a new irrigation water tariff approach for motorized and non-motorized pumping stations. 
4.	Improve the professional knowledge and experience of 201 farmers on irrigation water conservation and agricultural technologies in the Almaty and Turkestan areas.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	A new national development plan for RSE Kazvodkhoz 2020-2030 was drawn up and adopted by the Water Resources Committee in June 2021. 
2.	RSE Kazvodkhoz Chairman has endorsed the concept of irrigation water automation in August 2021.
3.	Three new formulas for the irrigation water tariffing for motorized and non-motorized pumping stations have been developed and accepted by the Committee for Regulation of Natural Monopolies in August 2021. 
4.	Increased professional knowledge and experience of 201 farmers on irrigation water conservation and agricultural technologies in the Almaty and Turkestan regions through a nationwide farmer open day campaign and targeted training and workshops.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">One updated State Water Programme to sustain organizational structure and functions of RSE Kazvodkhoz.
One concept of PPP in Water and two master plan developed to ensure sustainable irrigation water supply mechanisms
at least one formula proposed for the new irrigation water Tariff developed and submitted to RSE Kazvodkhoz
Established two water extension centers
Enhanced the capacities and knowledge of 750 farmers through on line and inline training and workshop programmes.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">New State Water Management Programme 2020-2030 has been developed and endorsed by the Government of Kazakhstan.
One concept on private public partnership in irrigation Water sector and three master plans were developed and endorsed by the Chairman of the Water Resource Committee.
Three Tariff methodologies proposed by the project and submitted to the RSE Kazvodkhoz
Established two water extension centers in Almaty and Turkestan regions
Enhanced the capacities and knowledge of 750 farmers through 36 on-line training and workshop programmes in all six projects target regions.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
